<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco II Ordelaffi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1300–1374</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco II Ordelaffi was lord of Forlì and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesena">Cesena</a> and a leading Ghibelline of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a>. He defied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gil-alvarez-carrillo-de-albornoz">Cardinal Albornoz</a>'s campaign to restore papal rule for years, while his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cia-degli-ubaldini">Cia degli Ubaldini</a> defended Cesena in 1357 until forced to surrender. He gave up Forlì in 1359 and later served as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> captain, but his family recovered the city after his death.</p></div>
